rd Dowling","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11056","person_slug":"richard-dowling","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sean Bell","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11062","person_slug":"sean-bell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tyron Whitten","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11060","person_slug":"tyron-whitten","vote":"no"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"}],"name":"Committees — Environment and Communications References Committee; Reference","noes":31,"question":"Steph Hodgins-May Well, here we go again—another day in this parliament, another game of 'guess who this government is working for'. Whether it's gambling reform, whether it's taxing our gas exports or whether it's this issue—multinational gas and other fossil fuel companies infiltrating our schools, our early learning centres and our public institutions to brainwash our kids—the answer is that this government is not working for you and it is not working for those families and teachers who are incredulous that this has been permitted to occur under this government's watch. When we first got wind of the fact that fossil fuel corporations—coal and gas corporations—were being allowed to brainwash children as young as six months old in early learning centres, we were stunned. Surely Labor would be as outraged as we were that this was being permitted to happen in our childcare centres and schools? Sadly, no—or, if they were shocked or disgusted, they hid it incredibly well. Now we are back in this place and we are giving Labor another shot to show who they are here to represent. Are they here to represent the gambling lobby that donates to them? Are they here to represent the fossil fuel industry that donates to them? Or are they here to represent Australian families and children? Labor will have a very, very simple choice in front of them in a matter of minutes: to support an inquiry into the influence of multinational coal and gas corporations on Australian children, or not to. That is the proposition that we are here to talk about today. It's a pretty simple one. It's a chance to ask some very basic questions of these fossil fuel polluters, of the education system, of the experts who know and understand the impacts of brainwashing children as young as six months old. How much money are fossil fuel corporations spending to influence children? How many programs are they running? How many schools? How many early learning centres? How many sporting clubs? How many communi","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10655","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-08-11/6"}
